WEBVTT

00:26:29.871 --> 00:26:32.038
you need to make it through
in order to keep going.

00:26:32.204 --> 00:26:34.871
Maybe your kill signal is we don't
want to have to tackle

00:26:35.746 --> 00:26:36.746
huge regulatory problems.

00:26:36.746 --> 00:26:40.204
That seems like something every team
should do in every workplace.

00:26:40.413 --> 00:26:43.954
Yeah, I mean, even just thinking about
what would your kill signal be,

00:26:44.288 --> 00:26:46.746
it tells you a lot about the problem
you're trying to solve.

00:26:47.038 --> 00:26:50.371
It also seems like it's more it
has broader applications.

00:26:50.371 --> 00:26:55.913
So I should I should take a new job
and have a kill signal around.

00:26:55.954 --> 00:26:58.538
OK, here's what would need
to happen in order

00:26:58.538 --> 00:27:01.496
for me to decide that it's
time to leave this job